{ "answer": ["LSD","acid","lysergic acid diethylamide"], "clues": ["Project MKUltra was a top-secret CIA program that used this in research about mind control and behavior modification during the Cold War. Researchers secretly administered this substance to unsuspecting citizens in bars, hospitals, and prisons but did not find that it produced reliable mind control","During the 1950s, psychiatrists used this to stimulate mental states or accelerate psychotherapy, but amid rising public concern, the US criminalized this under the Controlled Substances Act of 1970, classifying it as a Schedule I substance","Unlike mane other Schedule I substances, this does not produce compulsive drug-seeking behavior and is not considered physically addictive. It structurally resembles serotonin and brain imaging research suggests it causes communication between areas of the brain that normally do not interact, leading to profound shifts in time and reality."] },
